Adapt GPcal to pocknix: discover the hardware at runtime, persist the result.

Upstream targets one board (RP5): it hardcodes /sys/module/retroid, the evdev
name "Retroid Pocket Gamepad" and the trigger axis codes that driver uses, and
it saves a bash script into ~/.config/autostart for the CFW to source at boot.
pocknix ships one package for every board, and nothing here would run that
script, so detection moves into Klib/Pocknix.py and Save writes the conf that
pocknix-gamepad-calibration.service replays.

